{"id":"ma-fig-003","s":"maths","t":"p1-02","lv":2,"q":"The graph shows $y=x^2-4x+c$ with turning point P. Use P to write $x^2-4x+c$ in completed square form and to find $c$.","o":["$(x-2)^2+3$, so $c=7$","$(x+2)^2-3$, so $c=1$","$(x-2)^2-3$, so $c=1$","$(x-4)^2-3$, so $c=13$"],"a":2,"x":"P is the minimum at $(2,-3)$, so the form is $(x-2)^2-3$. Expanding gives $x^2-4x+1$, so $c=1$. This agrees with the curve crossing the $y$-axis at 1.","w":["Took the sign of P's $y$-coordinate wrongly, writing $+3$ instead of $-3$.","Wrote the bracket as $(x+2)$ instead of $(x-2)$, taking the wrong sign for P's $x$-coordinate.","","Used the whole coefficient $-4$ in the bracket instead of half of it, so the turning point would be at $x=4$."],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[0,4],"y":[-4,4],"xstep":1,"ystep":1,"xlabel":"x","ylabel":"y","lines":[{"pts":[[0.0,1.0],[0.025,0.900625],[0.05,0.8025],[0.075,0.705625],[0.1,0.61],[0.125,0.515625],[0.15,0.4225],[0.175,0.330625],[0.2,0.24],[0.225,0.150625],[0.25,0.0625],[0.275,-0.024375],[0.3,-0.11],[0.325,-0.194375],[0.35,-0.2775],[0.375,-0.359375],[0.4,-0.44],[0.425,-0.519375],[0.45,-0.5975],[0.475,-0.674375],[0.5,-0.75],[0.525,-0.824375],[0.55,-0.8975],[0.575,-0.969375],[0.6,-1.04],[0.625,-1.109375],[0.65,-1.1775],[0.675,-1.244375],[0.7,-1.31],[0.725,-1.374375],[0.75,-1.4375],[0.775,-1.499375],[0.8,-1.56],[0.825,-1.619375],[0.85,-1.6775],[0.875,-1.734375],[0.9,-1.79],[0.925,-1.844375],[0.95,-1.8975],[0.975,-1.949375],[1.0,-2.0],[1.025,-2.049375],[1.05,-2.0975],[1.075,-2.144375],[1.1,-2.19],[1.125,-2.234375],[1.15,-2.2775],[1.175,-2.319375],[1.2,-2.36],[1.225,-2.399375],[1.25,-2.4375],[1.275,-2.474375],[1.3,-2.51],[1.325,-2.544375],[1.35,-2.5775],[1.375,-2.609375],[1.4,-2.64],[1.425,-2.669375],[1.45,-2.6975],[1.475,-2.724375],[1.5,-2.75],[1.525,-2.774375],[1.55,-2.7975],[1.575,-2.819375],[1.6,-2.84],[1.625,-2.859375],[1.65,-2.8775],[1.675,-2.894375],[1.7,-2.91],[1.725,-2.924375],[1.75,-2.9375],[1.775,-2.949375],[1.8,-2.96],[1.825,-2.969375],[1.85,-