{"id":"ma-fig-004","s":"maths","t":"p1-02","lv":3,"q":"The graph shows $y=x^2-2x-3$ and the dashed line $y=m$. Use the graph to state how many real roots $x^2-2x-3=m$ has and the value of its discriminant.","o":["Two real roots; discriminant is $40$","No real roots; discriminant is $-8$","Equal roots; discriminant is $0$","Two real roots; discriminant is $16$"],"a":1,"x":"The dashed line is $y=-6$, below the minimum at $-4$, so it never meets the curve. Rearranging gives $x^2-2x+3=0$, so $b^2-4ac=4-12=-8$. No real roots.","w":["Rearranged to $x^2-2x-9=0$ by subtracting $m$ with the wrong sign; the graph shows no intersections.","","Used the turning point's height of $-4$ as the line's value; the line is lower, so it does not touch the curve.","Used the curve's crossings of the $x$-axis, which solve $f(x)=0$, instead of the dashed line."],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[-2,4],"y":[-8,6],"xstep":1,"ystep":2,"xlabel":"x","ylabel":"y","lines":[{"pts":[[-2.0,5.0],[-1.9625,4.776406],[-1.925,4.555625],[-1.8875,4.337656],[-1.85,4.1225],[-1.8125,3.910156],[-1.775,3.700625],[-1.7375,3.493906],[-1.7,3.29],[-1.6625,3.088906],[-1.625,2.890625],[-1.5875,2.695156],[-1.55,2.5025],[-1.5125,2.312656],[-1.475,2.125625],[-1.4375,1.941406],[-1.4,1.76],[-1.3625,1.581406],[-1.325,1.405625],[-1.2875,1.232656],[-1.25,1.0625],[-1.2125,0.895156],[-1.175,0.730625],[-1.1375,0.568906],[-1.1,0.41],[-1.0625,0.253906],[-1.025,0.100625],[-0.9875,-0.049844],[-0.95,-0.1975],[-0.9125,-0.342344],[-0.875,-0.484375],[-0.8375,-0.623594],[-0.8,-0.76],[-0.7625,-0.893594],[-0.725,-1.024375],[-0.6875,-1.152344],[-0.65,-1.2775],[-0.6125,-1.399844],[-0.575,-1.519375],[-0.5375,-1.636094],[-0.5,-1.75],[-0.4625,-1.861094],[-0.425,-1.969375],[-0.3875,-2.074844],[-0.35,-2.1775],[-0.3125,-2.277344],[-0.275,-2.374375],[-0.2375,-2.468594],[-0.2,-2.56],[-0.1625,-2.648594],[-0.125,-2.734375],[-0.0875,-2.817344],[-0.05,-2.8975],[-0.0125,-2.974844],[0.025,-3.049375],[0.0625,-3.121094],[0.1,-3.19],[0.1375,-3.256094],[0.175,-3.319