{"id":"ma-fig-021","s":"maths","t":"p1-09","lv":2,"q":"The graph shows the area of a triangle with sides $6$ cm and $b$ cm as the angle $\\theta$ between them varies. Use the graph to find $b$.","o":["$4$ cm","$8$ cm","$10$ cm","$48$ cm"],"a":1,"x":"The area is greatest when $\\sin\\theta=1$, at $\\theta=90^\\circ$, where the graph reads $24$ cm². So $\\frac12(6)(b)(1)=24$, giving $3b=24$ and $b=8$ cm.","w":["Uses area $=6b\\sin\\theta$, forgetting the factor $\\frac12$, so $6b=24$ and $b=4$.","","Assumes the maximum area is a right-angled triangle and finds the hypotenuse $\\sqrt{6^2+8^2}$ instead of the side $b$.","Writes $\\frac12 b=24$, leaving out the $6$ cm side, and gets $b=48$."],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[0,180],"y":[0,28],"xstep":30,"ystep":4,"xlabel":"angle θ / °","ylabel":"area / cm²","lines":[{"pts":[[0.0,0.0],[1.125,0.471209],[2.25,0.942236],[3.375,1.412899],[4.5,1.883018],[5.625,2.352411],[6.75,2.820898],[7.875,3.288296],[9.0,3.754427],[10.125,4.219111],[11.25,4.682168],[12.375,5.14342],[13.5,5.602689],[14.625,6.059798],[15.75,6.514571],[16.875,6.966832],[18.0,7.416408],[19.125,7.863124],[20.25,8.306809],[21.375,8.747292],[22.5,9.184402],[23.625,9.617972],[24.75,10.047834],[25.875,10.473822],[27.0,10.895772],[28.125,11.313522],[29.25,11.72691],[30.375,12.135777],[31.5,12.539966],[32.625,12.93932],[33.75,13.333686],[34.875,13.722911],[36.0,14.106846],[37.125,14.485343],[38.25,14.858255],[39.375,15.225439],[40.5,15.586753],[41.625,15.942059],[42.75,16.291218],[43.875,16.634097],[45.0,16.970563],[46.125,17.300486],[47.25,17.62374],[48.375,17.9402],[49.5,18.249743],[50.625,18.552251],[51.75,18.847606],[52.875,19.135696],[54.0,19.416408],[55.125,19.689635],[56.25,19.955271],[57.375,20.213214],[58.5,20.463364],[59.625,20.705625],[60.75,20.939904],[61.875,21.16611],[63.0,21.384157],[64.125,21.593959],[65.25,21.795436],[66.375,21.988511],[67.5,22.173109],[68.625,22.349158],[69.75,22.516592],[70.875,22.675345],[72.0,22.825356],[73.125,22.966568],[74.25,23.0989