{"id":"ma-fig-015","s":"maths","t":"p1-04","lv":2,"q":"The graph shows a curve C and a straight line L. Use the graph to find the values of $x$ for which C lies below L.","o":["$-2<x<4$","$x<-2$ or $x>4$","$-2<x<2$","$x<4$"],"a":0,"x":"The curve and line meet at $x=-2$ and $x=4$. Between these $x$-values the curve is below the line, for example at $x=0$ where C is lower than L. So $-2<x<4$.","w":["","Gives the values where C is above L, which reverses the inequality.","Uses the points where C crosses the $x$-axis rather than where it meets L.","Uses only the right-hand intersection and ignores the one at $x=-2$."],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[-3,5],"y":[-4,24],"xstep":1,"ystep":4,"xlabel":"x","ylabel":"y","lines":[{"pts":[[-3.0,5.0],[-2.95,4.7025],[-2.9,4.41],[-2.85,4.1225],[-2.8,3.84],[-2.75,3.5625],[-2.7,3.29],[-2.65,3.0225],[-2.6,2.76],[-2.55,2.5025],[-2.5,2.25],[-2.45,2.0025],[-2.4,1.76],[-2.35,1.5225],[-2.3,1.29],[-2.25,1.0625],[-2.2,0.84],[-2.15,0.6225],[-2.1,0.41],[-2.05,0.2025],[-2.0,0.0],[-1.95,-0.1975],[-1.9,-0.39],[-1.85,-0.5775],[-1.8,-0.76],[-1.75,-0.9375],[-1.7,-1.11],[-1.65,-1.2775],[-1.6,-1.44],[-1.55,-1.5975],[-1.5,-1.75],[-1.45,-1.8975],[-1.4,-2.04],[-1.35,-2.1775],[-1.3,-2.31],[-1.25,-2.4375],[-1.2,-2.56],[-1.15,-2.6775],[-1.1,-2.79],[-1.05,-2.8975],[-1.0,-3.0],[-0.95,-3.0975],[-0.9,-3.19],[-0.85,-3.2775],[-0.8,-3.36],[-0.75,-3.4375],[-0.7,-3.51],[-0.65,-3.5775],[-0.6,-3.64],[-0.55,-3.6975],[-0.5,-3.75],[-0.45,-3.7975],[-0.4,-3.84],[-0.35,-3.8775],[-0.3,-3.91],[-0.25,-3.9375],[-0.2,-3.96],[-0.15,-3.9775],[-0.1,-3.99],[-0.05,-3.9975],[0.0,-4.0],[0.05,-3.9975],[0.1,-3.99],[0.15,-3.9775],[0.2,-3.96],[0.25,-3.9375],[0.3,-3.91],[0.35,-3.8775],[0.4,-3.84],[0.45,-3.7975],[0.5,-3.75],[0.55,-3.6975],[0.6,-3.64],[0.65,-3.5775],[0.7,-3.51],[0.75,-3.4375],[0.8,-3.36],[0.85,-3.2775],[0.9,-3.19],[0.95,-3.0975],[1.0,-3.0],[1.05,-2.8975],[1.1,-2.79],[1.15,-2.6775],[1.2,-2.56],[1.25,-2.4375],[1.3,-2.31],[1.35,-2.1775],[1.4,-2.04],[1.45,-1.8975],[1.5,-1.75],[1.55,-1.