{"id":"ma-fig-016","s":"maths","t":"p1-04","lv":3,"q":"The graph shows curve A and curve B. B is the image of A under a single transformation. Which transformation maps A onto B?","o":["Stretch, scale factor 2, parallel to the $y$-axis","Stretch, scale factor $\\frac{1}{2}$, parallel to the $x$-axis","Stretch, scale factor $\\frac{1}{2}$, parallel to the $y$-axis","Stretch, scale factor 2, parallel to the $x$-axis"],"a":3,"x":"A crosses the $x$-axis at $\\pm2$ and B at $\\pm4$, and both have minimum $y=-4$. The $x$-values double and the $y$-values are unchanged: stretch scale factor 2 parallel to the $x$-axis, $y=f(\\frac{x}{2})$.","w":["A stretch parallel to the $y$-axis would keep the roots and change the minimum value, which stays at $-4$ here.","Takes the factor inside $f(\\tfrac{x}{2})$ as $\\tfrac12$ instead of 2, so the stretch is the wrong way round.","Uses the wrong direction and the wrong factor. The $y$-values do not change between A and B.",""],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[-6,6],"y":[-4,6],"xstep":2,"ystep":2,"xlabel":"x","ylabel":"y","lines":[{"pts":[[-3,5],[-2.5,2.25],[-2,0],[-1.5,-1.75],[-1,-3],[-0.5,-3.75],[0,-4],[0.5,-3.75],[1,-3],[1.5,-1.75],[2,0],[2.5,2.25],[3,5]],"label":"A","c":0},{"pts":[[-6,5],[-5,2.25],[-4,0],[-3,-1.75],[-2,-3],[-1,-3.75],[0,-4],[1,-3.75],[2,-3],[3,-1.75],[4,0],[5,2.25],[6,5]],"label":"B","c":1}],"xnums":true,"ynums":true}}
{"id":"ma-fig-017","s":"maths","t":"p1-04","lv":3,"q":"The graph shows $y=f(x)$, a transformation of $y=\\frac{1}{x}$, passing through the marked point P. Use the asymptotes and P to choose the equation of the graph.","o":["$y=\\frac{2}{x+1}+1$","$y=\\frac{2}{x-1}+1$","$y=\\frac{1}{x-1}+1$","$y=\\frac{2}{x-1}-1$"],"a":1,"x":"The branches approach $x=1$ and $y=1$, so the form is $y=\\frac{k}{x-1}+1$. P is $(2,3)$, so $3=\\frac{k}{1}+1$, giving $k=2$. The equation is $y=\\frac{2}{x-1}+1$.","w":["Shifts left to $x=-1$ instead of right to $x=1$. The vertical asymptote on the graph is at $x=1$.","","Gets both asymptotes right but takes $k=1$. At $x=2$ this gives $y=2$, not the $y$ of P.","Puts the horizontal asymptote at $y=-1$. The graph approaches $y=1$, which needs $+1$."],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[-3,5],"y":[-3,6],"xstep":1,"ystep":1,"xlabel":"x","ylabel":"y","lines":[{"pts":[[1.4,6],[1.5,5],[1.6,4.33],[1.75,3.67],[2,3],[2.5,2.33],[3,2],[4,1.67],[5,1.5]],"c":0},{"pts":[[-3,0.5],[-2,0.33],[-1,0],[-0.5,-0.33],[0,-1],[0.25,-1.67],[0.4,-2.33],[0.5,-3]],"c":1}],"points":[{"at":[2,3],"label":"P"}],"xnums":true,"ynums":true}}
{"id":"ma-fig-053","s":"maths","t":"p2-09","lv":2,"q":"The graph shows the gradient function $y=f'(x)$ of a curve $y=f(x)$. What does the graph show about $y=f(x)$ at the $x$-value of the labelled point P?","o":["A maximum point, since $f'(x)$ is greatest there","A stationary point, since the graph is flat there","A point of inflection, since $f''(x)=0$ and changes sign","A minimum point, since $f'(x)$ is positive there"],"a":2,"x":"The gradient of the graph is $f''(x)$. At P the graph has a maximum, so $f''(x)=0$ and changes from positive to negative. Since $f'(x)=1\\neq0$ there, $f$ has a non-stationary point of inflection.","w":["Read the maximum of $f'(x)$ as a maximum of $f(x)$. But $f$ has a maximum only where $f'$ crosses zero.","Treated a flat graph as stationary for $f$. The graph being flat means $f''=0$, not $f'=0$.","","Thought positive $f'(x)$ means a minimum. Positive $f'$ only tells us that $f$ is increasing."],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[0,6],"y":[0,1.5],"xstep":1,"ystep":0.25,"xlabel":"x","ylabel":"f'(x)","lines":[{"pts":[[0.0,0.0],[0.0375,0.002502],[0.075,0.00964],[0.1125,0.020892],[0.15,0.035775],[0.1875,0.053841],[0.225,0.074677],[0.2625,0.097902],[0.3,0.123166],[0.3375,0.150145],[0.375,0.178542],[0.4125,0.208084],[0.45,0.238523],[0.4875,0.26963],[0.525,0.301198],[0.5625,0.333037],[0.6,0.364975],[0.6375,0.396858],[0.675,0.428545],[0.7125,0.459909],[0.75,0.490839],[0.7875,0.521233],[0.825,0.551001],[0.8625,0.580065],[0.9,0.608355],[0.9375,0.635812],[0.975,0.662384],[1.0125,0.688025],[1.05,0.7127],[1.0875,0.736378],[1.125,0.759034],[1.1625,0.780649],[1.2,0.80121],[1.2375,0.820708],[1.275,0.839136],[1.3125,0.856494],[1.35,0.872785],[1.3875,0.888014],[1.425,0.902189],[1.4625,0.915321],[1.5,0.927424],[1.5375,0.938512],[1.575,0.948604],[1.6125,0.957717],[1.65,0.965872],[1.6875,0.97309],[1.725,0.979394],[1.7625,0.984808],[1.8,0.989356],[1.8375,0.993061],[1.875,0.995951],[1.9125,0.99805],[1.95,0.999384],[1.9875,0.99998],[2.025,0.999865],[2.0625,0.999063],