{"id":"ma-fig-023","s":"maths","t":"p1-12","lv":2,"q":"The graph shows a cubic curve $y=f(x)$. For which values of $k$ does the equation $f(x)=k$ have three distinct real roots?","o":["$-2<k<2$","$-16\\le k\\le 16$","$k<-16$ or $k>16$","$-16<k<16$"],"a":3,"x":"The turning points are at $(-2,16)$ (maximum) and $(2,-16)$ (minimum). The horizontal line $y=k$ cuts the curve three times only when it lies strictly between the minimum and maximum values: $-16<k<16$.","w":["Used the $x$-coordinates of the turning points instead of their $y$-values.","At $k=\\pm16$ the line touches a turning point, giving a repeated root, so only two distinct roots.","This range gives only one intersection, since the line is beyond both turning values.",""],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[-4,4],"y":[-24,24],"xstep":1,"ystep":8,"xlabel":"x","ylabel":"y","lines":[{"pts":[[-4.0,-16.0],[-3.95,-14.229875],[-3.9,-12.519],[-3.85,-10.866625],[-3.8,-9.272],[-3.75,-7.734375],[-3.7,-6.253],[-3.65,-4.827125],[-3.6,-3.456],[-3.55,-2.138875],[-3.5,-0.875],[-3.45,0.336375],[-3.4,1.496],[-3.35,2.604625],[-3.3,3.663],[-3.25,4.671875],[-3.2,5.632],[-3.15,6.544125],[-3.1,7.409],[-3.05,8.227375],[-3.0,9.0],[-2.95,9.727625],[-2.9,10.411],[-2.85,11.050875],[-2.8,11.648],[-2.75,12.203125],[-2.7,12.717],[-2.65,13.190375],[-2.6,13.624],[-2.55,14.018625],[-2.5,14.375],[-2.45,14.693875],[-2.4,14.976],[-2.35,15.222125],[-2.3,15.433],[-2.25,15.609375],[-2.2,15.752],[-2.15,15.861625],[-2.1,15.939],[-2.05,15.984875],[-2.0,16.0],[-1.95,15.985125],[-1.9,15.941],[-1.85,15.868375],[-1.8,15.768],[-1.75,15.640625],[-1.7,15.487],[-1.65,15.307875],[-1.6,15.104],[-1.55,14.876125],[-1.5,14.625],[-1.45,14.351375],[-1.4,14.056],[-1.35,13.739625],[-1.3,13.403],[-1.25,13.046875],[-1.2,12.672],[-1.15,12.279125],[-1.1,11.869],[-1.05,11.442375],[-1.0,11.0],[-0.95,10.542625],[-0.9,10.071],[-0.85,9.585875],[-0.8,9.088],[-0.75,8.578125],[-0.7,8.057],[-0.65,7.525375],[-0.6,6.984],[-0.55,6.433625],[-0.5,5.875],[-0.45,5.308875],[-0.4,4.736],[-0.35,4