{"id":"ma-fig-024","s":"maths","t":"p1-12","lv":3,"q":"The graph shows the gradient of the chord from $x=2$ to $x=2+h$ against $h$, for a curve $y=f(x)$ with $f(2)=8$. Which option is the equation of the tangent to the curve at $x=2$?","o":["$y=12x-16$","$y=28x-48$","$y=12x+8$","$y=-\\frac{1}{12}x+\\frac{49}{6}$"],"a":0,"x":"As $h\\to0$ the chord gradient approaches the value where the graph meets the vertical axis, 12. So $f'(2)=12$. Tangent: $y-8=12(x-2)$, giving $y=12x-16$.","w":["","Read the chord gradient at the right-hand end ($h=2$) instead of the limit as $h\\to0$.","Used the correct gradient but took $f(2)=8$ as the $y$-intercept.","Found the normal, using the negative reciprocal of the limiting gradient."],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[-1,2],"y":[4,28],"xstep":0.5,"ystep":4,"xlabel":"h","ylabel":"gradient of chord","lines":[{"pts":[[-1.0,7.0],[-0.98125,7.075352],[-0.9625,7.151406],[-0.94375,7.228164],[-0.925,7.305625],[-0.90625,7.383789],[-0.8875,7.462656],[-0.86875,7.542227],[-0.85,7.6225],[-0.83125,7.703477],[-0.8125,7.785156],[-0.79375,7.867539],[-0.775,7.950625],[-0.75625,8.034414],[-0.7375,8.118906],[-0.71875,8.204102],[-0.7,8.29],[-0.68125,8.376602],[-0.6625,8.463906],[-0.64375,8.551914],[-0.625,8.640625],[-0.60625,8.730039],[-0.5875,8.820156],[-0.56875,8.910977],[-0.55,9.0025],[-0.53125,9.094727],[-0.5125,9.187656],[-0.49375,9.281289],[-0.475,9.375625],[-0.45625,9.470664],[-0.4375,9.566406],[-0.41875,9.662852],[-0.4,9.76],[-0.38125,9.857852],[-0.3625,9.956406],[-0.34375,10.055664],[-0.325,10.155625],[-0.30625,10.256289],[-0.2875,10.357656],[-0.26875,10.459727],[-0.25,10.5625],[-0.23125,10.665977],[-0.2125,10.770156],[-0.19375,10.875039],[-0.175,10.980625],[-0.15625,11.086914],[-0.1375,11.193906],[-0.11875,11.301602],[-0.1,11.41],[-0.08125,11.519102],[-0.0625,11.628906],[-0.04375,11.739414],[-0.025,11.850625],[-0.00625,11.962539],[0.0125,12.075156],[0.03125,12.188477],[0.05,12.3025],[0.06875,12.417227],[0.0875,12.532656],[0.10625,12.648789],[0.125,12.76