{"id":"ma-fig-026","s":"maths","t":"p1-13","lv":2,"q":"The graph shows the curve $y=\\mathrm{f}(x)$, where $\\mathrm{f}'(x)=3x^2-4$. The point P lies on the curve. Find $\\mathrm{f}(x)$.","o":["$x^3-4x+2$","$x^3-4x-1$","$x^3-4x+7$","$x^3-4x+5$"],"a":3,"x":"$\\mathrm{f}(x)=x^3-4x+c$. P is $(1,2)$, so $1-4+c=2$, giving $c=5$. So $\\mathrm{f}(x)=x^3-4x+5$.","w":["Took $c$ to be the $y$-coordinate of P without substituting $x=1$ into $x^3-4x$.","Added $-3$ to $2$ instead of subtracting it: $c=2+(1-4)$.","Added both $1$ and $4$ to the $y$-value, a sign slip when substituting $x=1$.",""],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[-2,2],"y":[0,10],"xstep":1,"ystep":2,"xlabel":"x","ylabel":"y","lines":[{"pts":[[-2.0,5.0],[-1.975,5.196266],[-1.95,5.385125],[-1.925,5.566672],[-1.9,5.741],[-1.875,5.908203],[-1.85,6.068375],[-1.825,6.221609],[-1.8,6.368],[-1.775,6.507641],[-1.75,6.640625],[-1.725,6.767047],[-1.7,6.887],[-1.675,7.000578],[-1.65,7.107875],[-1.625,7.208984],[-1.6,7.304],[-1.575,7.393016],[-1.55,7.476125],[-1.525,7.553422],[-1.5,7.625],[-1.475,7.690953],[-1.45,7.751375],[-1.425,7.806359],[-1.4,7.856],[-1.375,7.900391],[-1.35,7.939625],[-1.325,7.973797],[-1.3,8.003],[-1.275,8.027328],[-1.25,8.046875],[-1.225,8.061734],[-1.2,8.072],[-1.175,8.077766],[-1.15,8.079125],[-1.125,8.076172],[-1.1,8.069],[-1.075,8.057703],[-1.05,8.042375],[-1.025,8.023109],[-1.0,8.0],[-0.975,7.973141],[-0.95,7.942625],[-0.925,7.908547],[-0.9,7.871],[-0.875,7.830078],[-0.85,7.785875],[-0.825,7.738484],[-0.8,7.688],[-0.775,7.634516],[-0.75,7.578125],[-0.725,7.518922],[-0.7,7.457],[-0.675,7.392453],[-0.65,7.325375],[-0.625,7.255859],[-0.6,7.184],[-0.575,7.109891],[-0.55,7.033625],[-0.525,6.955297],[-0.5,6.875],[-0.475,6.792828],[-0.45,6.708875],[-0.425,6.623234],[-0.4,6.536],[-0.375,6.447266],[-0.35,6.357125],[-0.325,6.265672],[-0.3,6.173],[-0.275,6.079203],[-0.25,5.984375],[-0.225,5.888609],[-0.2,5.792],[-0.175,5.694641],[-0.15,5.596625],[-0.125,5.498047],[-0.1,5.399],[-0.075,5.299578],[-0.05,5.199875],[-0.02