{"id":"ma-fig-027","s":"maths","t":"p1-13","lv":3,"q":"The graph shows the curve $y=x^2$ and a straight line, meeting at A and B. Find the area of the region enclosed between the line and the curve.","o":["$\\frac92$","$\\frac{15}{2}$","$3$","$-\\frac92$"],"a":0,"x":"A is $(-1,1)$ and B is $(2,4)$, so the line has gradient $1$ and equation $y=x+2$. Area $=\\int_{-1}^{2}(x+2-x^2)\\,dx=\\left[\\frac{x^2}{2}+2x-\\frac{x^3}{3}\\right]_{-1}^{2}=\\frac92$.","w":["","Found only the area under the line between A and B, forgetting to subtract the area under the curve.","Found only the area under the curve $y=x^2$ between the $x$-values of A and B.","Subtracted the wrong way round, curve minus line, which gives a negative value."],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[-2,3],"y":[0,9],"xstep":1,"ystep":1,"xlabel":"x","ylabel":"y","lines":[{"pts":[[-2.0,4.0],[-1.96875,3.875977],[-1.9375,3.753906],[-1.90625,3.633789],[-1.875,3.515625],[-1.84375,3.399414],[-1.8125,3.285156],[-1.78125,3.172852],[-1.75,3.0625],[-1.71875,2.954102],[-1.6875,2.847656],[-1.65625,2.743164],[-1.625,2.640625],[-1.59375,2.540039],[-1.5625,2.441406],[-1.53125,2.344727],[-1.5,2.25],[-1.46875,2.157227],[-1.4375,2.066406],[-1.40625,1.977539],[-1.375,1.890625],[-1.34375,1.805664],[-1.3125,1.722656],[-1.28125,1.641602],[-1.25,1.5625],[-1.21875,1.485352],[-1.1875,1.410156],[-1.15625,1.336914],[-1.125,1.265625],[-1.09375,1.196289],[-1.0625,1.128906],[-1.03125,1.063477],[-1.0,1.0],[-0.96875,0.938477],[-0.9375,0.878906],[-0.90625,0.821289],[-0.875,0.765625],[-0.84375,0.711914],[-0.8125,0.660156],[-0.78125,0.610352],[-0.75,0.5625],[-0.71875,0.516602],[-0.6875,0.472656],[-0.65625,0.430664],[-0.625,0.390625],[-0.59375,0.352539],[-0.5625,0.316406],[-0.53125,0.282227],[-0.5,0.25],[-0.46875,0.219727],[-0.4375,0.191406],[-0.40625,0.165039],[-0.375,0.140625],[-0.34375,0.118164],[-0.3125,0.097656],[-0.28125,0.079102],[-0.25,0.0625],[-0.21875,0.047852],[-0.1875,0.035156],[-0.15625,0.024414],[-0.125,0.015625],[-0.09375,0.008789],[-0.0625