{"id":"ma-fig-028","s":"maths","t":"p1-13","lv":3,"q":"The graph shows $y=\\mathrm{f}(x)$, where $\\mathrm{f}$ is a cubic whose $x^3$ coefficient is $1$. Find the total area enclosed between the curve and the $x$-axis.","o":["$0$","$4$","$8$","$16$"],"a":2,"x":"The roots are $0$, $2$, $4$, so $\\mathrm{f}(x)=x^3-6x^2+8x$. $\\int_0^2=4$ and $\\int_2^4=-4$. The curve is above the axis, then below it, so total area $=4+4=8$.","w":["Found $\\int_0^4\\mathrm{f}(x)\\,dx$, where the positive and negative parts cancel. Area needs each part made positive.","Found the area of only one of the two loops.","","Doubled the total area again, counting both loops twice."],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[0,4],"y":[-4,4],"xstep":1,"ystep":1,"xlabel":"x","ylabel":"y","lines":[{"pts":[[0.0,0.0],[0.025,0.196266],[0.05,0.385125],[0.075,0.566672],[0.1,0.741],[0.125,0.908203],[0.15,1.068375],[0.175,1.221609],[0.2,1.368],[0.225,1.507641],[0.25,1.640625],[0.275,1.767047],[0.3,1.887],[0.325,2.000578],[0.35,2.107875],[0.375,2.208984],[0.4,2.304],[0.425,2.393016],[0.45,2.476125],[0.475,2.553422],[0.5,2.625],[0.525,2.690953],[0.55,2.751375],[0.575,2.806359],[0.6,2.856],[0.625,2.900391],[0.65,2.939625],[0.675,2.973797],[0.7,3.003],[0.725,3.027328],[0.75,3.046875],[0.775,3.061734],[0.8,3.072],[0.825,3.077766],[0.85,3.079125],[0.875,3.076172],[0.9,3.069],[0.925,3.057703],[0.95,3.042375],[0.975,3.023109],[1.0,3.0],[1.025,2.973141],[1.05,2.942625],[1.075,2.908547],[1.1,2.871],[1.125,2.830078],[1.15,2.785875],[1.175,2.738484],[1.2,2.688],[1.225,2.634516],[1.25,2.578125],[1.275,2.518922],[1.3,2.457],[1.325,2.392453],[1.35,2.325375],[1.375,2.255859],[1.4,2.184],[1.425,2.109891],[1.45,2.033625],[1.475,1.955297],[1.5,1.875],[1.525,1.792828],[1.55,1.708875],[1.575,1.623234],[1.6,1.536],[1.625,1.447266],[1.65,1.357125],[1.675,1.265672],[1.7,1.173],[1.725,1.079203],[1.75,0.984375],[1.775,0.888609],[1.8,0.792],[1.825,0.694641],[1.85,0.596625],[1.875,0.498047],[1.9,0.399],[1.925,0.299578],[1.95,0.199875],[1.975,0.09