{"id":"ma-fig-059","s":"maths","t":"s2-01","lv":3,"q":"The graph shows $\\log_{10}y$ against $\\log_{10}x$ for some data, with the points lying on a straight line. Which model for $y$ in terms of $x$ is suggested by the graph?","o":["$y=1.5x^{10}$","$y=10x^{1.5}$","$y=10^{1.5}x$","$y=10\\times1.5^{x}$"],"a":1,"x":"The line passes through P(0, 1) and Q(2, 4), so the gradient is $(4-1)/2=1.5$ and the intercept is 1. From $\\log y=\\log a+n\\log x$: $n=1.5$ and $a=10^1=10$. So $y=10x^{1.5}$.","w":["Used the gradient as $a$ and took $10^{\\text{intercept}}$ as the power, so the roles of gradient and intercept are swapped.","","Put the gradient into the constant by writing $10^{1.5}$ as the multiplier, instead of using it as the power of $x$.","Treated the graph as $\\log y$ against $x$ (an exponential model), so used 1.5 directly as the base $b$."],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[0,3],"y":[0,6],"xstep":0.5,"ystep":1,"xlabel":"log₁₀ x","ylabel":"log₁₀ y","lines":[{"pts":[[0.0,1.0],[0.01875,1.028125],[0.0375,1.05625],[0.05625,1.084375],[0.075,1.1125],[0.09375,1.140625],[0.1125,1.16875],[0.13125,1.196875],[0.15,1.225],[0.16875,1.253125],[0.1875,1.28125],[0.20625,1.309375],[0.225,1.3375],[0.24375,1.365625],[0.2625,1.39375],[0.28125,1.421875],[0.3,1.45],[0.31875,1.478125],[0.3375,1.50625],[0.35625,1.534375],[0.375,1.5625],[0.39375,1.590625],[0.4125,1.61875],[0.43125,1.646875],[0.45,1.675],[0.46875,1.703125],[0.4875,1.73125],[0.50625,1.759375],[0.525,1.7875],[0.54375,1.815625],[0.5625,1.84375],[0.58125,1.871875],[0.6,1.9],[0.61875,1.928125],[0.6375,1.95625],[0.65625,1.984375],[0.675,2.0125],[0.69375,2.040625],[0.7125,2.06875],[0.73125,2.096875],[0.75,2.125],[0.76875,2.153125],[0.7875,2.18125],[0.80625,2.209375],[0.825,2.2375],[0.84375,2.265625],[0.8625,2.29375],[0.88125,2.321875],[0.9,2.35],[0.91875,2.378125],[0.9375,2.40625],[0.95625,2.434375],[0.975,2.4625],[0.99375,2.490625],[1.0125,2.51875],[1.03125,2.546875],[1.05,2.575],[1.06875,2.603125],[1.0875,2.63125],[1.10625,2.659375],