{"id":"ma-fig-009","s":"maths","t":"p1-02","lv":2,"q":"The graph shows a quadratic curve through the marked points P, Q and R. Which equation gives the curve?","o":["$y=x^2+2x-3$","$y=2x^2+4x-6$","$y=2x^2-4x-6$","$y=2x^2+2x-6$"],"a":1,"x":"The curve crosses the x-axis at $x=-3$ and $x=1$, so $y=a(x+3)(x-1)$. At R, $x=0$ and $y=-6$, so $-3a=-6$ and $a=2$. Expanding gives $y=2x^2+4x-6$.","w":["Uses the roots correctly but ignores the y-intercept at R, so takes $a=1$ and gets $y=-3$ at $x=0$.","","Takes the roots as $x=3$ and $x=-1$, reversing the signs of the roots, which flips the sign of the $x$ term.","Finds $a=2$ but multiplies out wrongly, doubling only the $x^2$ and constant terms and not the $x$ term."],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[-4,2],"y":[-8,10],"xstep":1,"ystep":2,"xlabel":"x","ylabel":"y","lines":[{"pts":[[-4.0,10.0],[-3.9625,9.552812],[-3.925,9.11125],[-3.8875,8.675313],[-3.85,8.245],[-3.8125,7.820312],[-3.775,7.40125],[-3.7375,6.987812],[-3.7,6.58],[-3.6625,6.177812],[-3.625,5.78125],[-3.5875,5.390312],[-3.55,5.005],[-3.5125,4.625313],[-3.475,4.25125],[-3.4375,3.882812],[-3.4,3.52],[-3.3625,3.162812],[-3.325,2.81125],[-3.2875,2.465313],[-3.25,2.125],[-3.2125,1.790313],[-3.175,1.46125],[-3.1375,1.137813],[-3.1,0.82],[-3.0625,0.507812],[-3.025,0.20125],[-2.9875,-0.099688],[-2.95,-0.395],[-2.9125,-0.684688],[-2.875,-0.96875],[-2.8375,-1.247188],[-2.8,-1.52],[-2.7625,-1.787187],[-2.725,-2.04875],[-2.6875,-2.304688],[-2.65,-2.555],[-2.6125,-2.799688],[-2.575,-3.03875],[-2.5375,-3.272187],[-2.5,-3.5],[-2.4625,-3.722188],[-2.425,-3.93875],[-2.3875,-4.149687],[-2.35,-4.355],[-2.3125,-4.554688],[-2.275,-4.74875],[-2.2375,-4.937188],[-2.2,-5.12],[-2.1625,-5.297187],[-2.125,-5.46875],[-2.0875,-5.634688],[-2.05,-5.795],[-2.0125,-5.949687],[-1.975,-6.09875],[-1.9375,-6.242188],[-1.9,-6.38],[-1.8625,-6.512188],[-1.825,-6.63875],[-1.7875,-6.759688],[-1.75,-6.875],[-1.7125,-6.984688],[-1.675,-7.08875],[-1.6375,-7.187187],[-1.6,-7.28],[-1.5625,-7.367188],[-1.525,-7.44875]