{"id":"ma-fig-010","s":"maths","t":"p1-02","lv":3,"q":"The graph shows the curve $y=x^2-4x+3$ and a line L through the marked points A and B. Use the graph to find the equation of L, then use the discriminant to say how L meets the curve.","o":["$y=\\tfrac{1}{2}x-6$; no points in common","$y=2x+6$; two points in common","$y=-2x-6$; no points in common","$y=2x-6$; one point of contact (tangent)"],"a":3,"x":"A is $(0,-6)$ and B is $(4,2)$, so the gradient is $8\\div4=2$ and $y=2x-6$. Equating: $x^2-6x+9=0$. The discriminant is $36-36=0$, so L touches the curve at one point.","w":["Finds the gradient as run over rise, $4\\div8$, giving $\\tfrac12$; the discriminant is then negative.","Reads the intercept at A as $+6$ instead of $-6$; this gives a positive discriminant and two points.","Gets the sign of the gradient wrong, although L slopes upwards; the discriminant is then negative.",""],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[-1,5],"y":[-6,8],"xstep":1,"ystep":2,"xlabel":"x","ylabel":"y","lines":[{"pts":[[-1.0,8.0],[-0.9625,7.776406],[-0.925,7.555625],[-0.8875,7.337656],[-0.85,7.1225],[-0.8125,6.910156],[-0.775,6.700625],[-0.7375,6.493906],[-0.7,6.29],[-0.6625,6.088906],[-0.625,5.890625],[-0.5875,5.695156],[-0.55,5.5025],[-0.5125,5.312656],[-0.475,5.125625],[-0.4375,4.941406],[-0.4,4.76],[-0.3625,4.581406],[-0.325,4.405625],[-0.2875,4.232656],[-0.25,4.0625],[-0.2125,3.895156],[-0.175,3.730625],[-0.1375,3.568906],[-0.1,3.41],[-0.0625,3.253906],[-0.025,3.100625],[0.0125,2.950156],[0.05,2.8025],[0.0875,2.657656],[0.125,2.515625],[0.1625,2.376406],[0.2,2.24],[0.2375,2.106406],[0.275,1.975625],[0.3125,1.847656],[0.35,1.7225],[0.3875,1.600156],[0.425,1.480625],[0.4625,1.363906],[0.5,1.25],[0.5375,1.138906],[0.575,1.030625],[0.6125,0.925156],[0.65,0.8225],[0.6875,0.722656],[0.725,0.625625],[0.7625,0.531406],[0.8,0.44],[0.8375,0.351406],[0.875,0.265625],[0.9125,0.182656],[0.95,0.1025],[0.9875,0.025156],[1.025,-0.049375],[1.0625,-0.121094],[1.1,-0.19],[1.1375,-0.256094],[1.175,-0.319375],[