{"id":"ma-fig-062","s":"maths","t":"m2-06","lv":3,"q":"The graph shows a ball's height against time. It lands 60 m horizontally from the launch point. Taking $g=9.8$, what is the angle of projection above the horizontal?","o":["33.2°","37.4°","69.1°","52.6°"],"a":3,"x":"The ball lands at L, $t=4$ s. It rises for 2 s, so $u_y=9.8\\times2=19.6$. Horizontally $u_x=60\\div4=15$. Then $\\tan\\theta=19.6\\div15$, so $\\theta\\approx52.6^\\circ$.","w":["Read the time of the highest point (2 s) as the whole flight time, so $u_x=30$, while still using $u_y=19.6$.","Inverted the ratio, using $\\tan\\theta=15\\div19.6$ instead of vertical over horizontal.","Took $u_y=9.8\\times4$, using the whole flight time instead of the time to the highest point.",""],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[0,4],"y":[0,20],"xstep":0.5,"ystep":5,"xlabel":"time / s","ylabel":"height / m","lines":[{"pts":[[0.0,0.0],[0.025,0.486938],[0.05,0.96775],[0.075,1.442438],[0.1,1.911],[0.125,2.373438],[0.15,2.82975],[0.175,3.279937],[0.2,3.724],[0.225,4.161938],[0.25,4.59375],[0.275,5.019438],[0.3,5.439],[0.325,5.852438],[0.35,6.25975],[0.375,6.660938],[0.4,7.056],[0.425,7.444937],[0.45,7.82775],[0.475,8.204438],[0.5,8.575],[0.525,8.939438],[0.55,9.29775],[0.575,9.649938],[0.6,9.996],[0.625,10.335938],[0.65,10.66975],[0.675,10.997438],[0.7,11.319],[0.725,11.634438],[0.75,11.94375],[0.775,12.246938],[0.8,12.544],[0.825,12.834938],[0.85,13.11975],[0.875,13.398438],[0.9,13.671],[0.925,13.937438],[0.95,14.19775],[0.975,14.451937],[1.0,14.7],[1.025,14.941937],[1.05,15.17775],[1.075,15.407438],[1.1,15.631],[1.125,15.848437],[1.15,16.05975],[1.175,16.264937],[1.2,16.464],[1.225,16.656938],[1.25,16.84375],[1.275,17.024437],[1.3,17.199],[1.325,17.367438],[1.35,17.52975],[1.375,17.685938],[1.4,17.836],[1.425,17.979938],[1.45,18.11775],[1.475,18.249438],[1.5,18.375],[1.525,18.494438],[1.55,18.60775],[1.575,18.714938],[1.6,18.816],[1.625,18.910938],[1.65,18.99975],[1.675,19.082438],[1.7,19.159],[1.725,19.229437],[1.75,19.29375]