{"id":"ma-fig-018","s":"maths","t":"p1-05","lv":2,"q":"The graph shows line $l$ and point P. Line $m$ passes through P and is parallel to $l$. Which is the equation of $m$?","o":["$2x-3y+14=0$","$3x+2y-18=0$","$3x-2y+6=0$","$3x-2y-4=0$"],"a":2,"x":"Read $(0,-2)$ and $(4,4)$ on $l$: gradient $=\\frac{6}{4}=\\frac32$. Parallel lines share this gradient. Through P$(2,6)$: $y-6=\\frac32(x-2)$, so $3x-2y+6=0$.","w":["Uses the gradient upside down, $\\frac23$ instead of $\\frac32$, when working out the equation of $m$.","Uses gradient $-\\frac32$, the wrong sign, so the line slopes down instead of being parallel to $l$.","","Gives the equation of $l$ itself, using its intercept and gradient, instead of the line through P."],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[-2,6],"y":[-4,8],"xstep":1,"ystep":2,"xlabel":"x","ylabel":"y","lines":[{"pts":[[-1,-3.5],[5,5.5]],"label":"l","c":0}],"points":[{"at":[2,6],"label":"P"}],"xnums":true,"ynums":true}}
{"id":"ma-fig-019","s":"maths","t":"p1-05","lv":2,"q":"The graph shows the cost, $C$ pounds, of hiring a van for $d$ days from companies A and B. For which numbers of days is company A the cheaper option?","o":["$d>4$","$d<4$","$d<24$","$d<8$"],"a":1,"x":"The lines cross at $d=4$, $C=24$. Before this A's line is lower (it starts at 8, B's at 16). So A is cheaper when $d<4$.","w":["Picks the values where A's line is above B's, so mixes up which line is lower.","","Gives the cost at the crossing point, $C=24$, instead of the number of days read from the $d$-axis.","Uses A's intercept on the $C$-axis as the crossing point instead of the $d$-value where the lines meet."],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[0,8],"y":[0,48],"xstep":1,"ystep":8,"xlabel":"time, d / days","ylabel":"cost, C / £","lines":[{"pts":[[0,8],[8,40]],"label":"A","c":0},{"pts":[[0,16],[8,32]],"label":"B","c":1}],"xnums":true,"ynums":true}}
{"id":"ma-fig-056","s":"maths","t":"p2-11","lv":2,"q":"The graph shows the solution curve of $\\frac{dy}{dx}=ky$, where $k$ is a constant, passing through the marked points P and Q. Find the exact value of $k$.","o":["$\\ln 4$","$\\ln 2$","$\\frac{3}{2}$","$\\frac{\\ln 2}{2}$"],"a":1,"x":"Separating gives $y=Ae^{kx}$. P gives $A=3$. At Q, $x=2$ and $y=12$, so $e^{2k}=4$. Then $2k=\\ln 4$, so $k=\\ln 2$.","w":["Found $e^{2k}=4$ but forgot to divide by the $x$-value 2, giving $k=\\ln 4$.","","Used the average gradient $(12-3)/2=4.5$ divided by 3, which is not how $k$ arises in $y=Ae^{kx}$.","Divided by 2 twice, once when solving $2k=\\ln 4$ and again afterwards."],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[0,2],"y":[0,15],"xstep":0.5,"ystep":3,"xlabel":"x","ylabel":"y","lines":[{"pts":[[0.0,3.0],[0.0125,3.026106],[0.025,3.052439],[0.0375,3.079001],[0.05,3.105795],[0.0625,3.132821],[0.075,3.160083],[0.0875,3.187582],[0.1,3.21532],[0.1125,3.2433],[0.125,3.271523],[0.1375,3.299992],[0.15,3.328708],[0.1625,3.357675],[0.175,3.386893],[0.1875,3.416366],[0.2,3.446095],[0.2125,3.476083],[0.225,3.506332],[0.2375,3.536844],[0.25,3.567621],[0.2625,3.598667],[0.275,3.629982],[0.2875,3.66157],[0.3,3.693433],[0.3125,3.725573],[0.325,3.757993],[0.3375,3.790695],[0.35,3.823682],[0.3625,3.856955],[0.375,3.890519],[0.3875,3.924374],[0.4,3.958524],[0.4125,3.992971],[0.425,4.027718],[0.4375,4.062767],[0.45,4.098121],[0.4625,4.133783],[0.475,4.169755],[0.4875,4.20604],[0.5,4.242641],[0.5125,4.27956],[0.525,4.316801],[0.5375,4.354365],[0.55,4.392257],[0.5625,4.430478],[0.575,4.469032],[0.5875,4.507922],[0.6,4.54715],[0.6125,4.586719],[0.625,4.626632],[0.6375,4.666893],[0.65,4.707505],[0.6625,4.748469],[0.675,4.78979],[0.6875,4.831471],[0.7,4.873514],[0.7125,4.915924],[0.725,4.958702],[0.7375,5.001852],[0.75,5.045378],[0.7625,5.089283],[0.775,5.13357],[0.7875,5.178242],[0.8,5.223303],[0.8125,5.268756],[0.825,5.314605],[0.8375,5.360853],[0.85,5.407503],[0.8625,5.454559],[0.875,5.502024],[0.8875,5.549903],[0