{"id":"ma-fig-058","s":"maths","t":"p2-11","lv":3,"q":"The graph shows $y=\\frac{6}{(x+1)(x+2)}$. Use partial fractions to find the exact area between the curve and the x-axis, bounded by the vertical lines through P and Q.","o":["$6\\ln\\frac{3}{2}$","$6\\ln\\frac{4}{3}$","$\\ln\\frac{9}{8}$","$6\\ln\\frac{9}{8}$"],"a":3,"x":"The graph gives P at $x=1$ and Q at $x=2$. Now $\\frac{6}{(x+1)(x+2)}=\\frac{6}{x+1}-\\frac{6}{x+2}$. So area $=6\\left[\\ln\\frac{x+1}{x+2}\\right]_1^2=6\\left(\\ln\\frac34-\\ln\\frac23\\right)=6\\ln\\frac98$.","w":["Integrated only the $\\frac{6}{x+1}$ term and dropped $-\\frac{6}{x+2}$.","Used limits 0 and 1 instead of 1 and 2, misreading the x-coordinates of P and Q.","Lost the numerator 6 when splitting into partial fractions, so the area was not multiplied by 6.",""],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[0,4],"y":[0,3],"xstep":1,"ystep":0.5,"xlabel":"x","ylabel":"y","lines":[{"pts":[[0.0,3.0],[0.025,2.890696],[0.05,2.787456],[0.075,2.689829],[0.1,2.597403],[0.125,2.509804],[0.15,2.426694],[0.175,2.347762],[0.2,2.272727],[0.225,2.20133],[0.25,2.133333],[0.275,2.06852],[0.3,2.006689],[0.325,1.947657],[0.35,1.891253],[0.375,1.837321],[0.4,1.785714],[0.425,1.7363],[0.45,1.688951],[0.475,1.643554],[0.5,1.6],[0.525,1.558189],[0.55,1.518027],[0.575,1.479427],[0.6,1.442308],[0.625,1.406593],[0.65,1.372213],[0.675,1.339099],[0.7,1.30719],[0.725,1.276426],[0.75,1.246753],[0.775,1.21812],[0.8,1.190476],[0.825,1.163777],[0.85,1.13798],[0.875,1.113043],[0.9,1.088929],[0.925,1.065601],[0.95,1.043025],[0.975,1.021168],[1.0,1.0],[1.025,0.979492],[1.05,0.959616],[1.075,0.940347],[1.1,0.921659],[1.125,0.903529],[1.15,0.885936],[1.175,0.868857],[1.2,0.852273],[1.225,0.836164],[1.25,0.820513],[1.275,0.805302],[1.3,0.790514],[1.325,0.776134],[1.35,0.762147],[1.375,0.748538],[1.4,0.735294],[1.425,0.722402],[1.45,0.709849],[1.475,0.697624],[1.5,0.685714],[1.525,0.67411],[1.55,0.6628],[1.575,0.651775],[1.6,0.641026],[1.625,0.630542],[1.65,0.620315],[1.675,0.610338],[1.7,0