{"id":"ma-fig-041","s":"maths","t":"m1-11","lv":1,"q":"The graph shows the velocity of a particle moving in a straight line. At what time is the acceleration of the particle zero?","o":["$4$ s","$2$ s","$12$ s","$0$ s"],"a":1,"x":"Acceleration is the gradient of the velocity-time graph. The gradient is zero at the turning point P, the maximum, which is at $t=2$ s on the horizontal axis.","w":["Takes the time when $v=0$ again. The velocity is zero there but the gradient is not, so the acceleration is not zero.","","Reads the maximum velocity from the vertical axis and gives it as the time. The question asks for the time.","Takes the time when $v=0$ at the start. The gradient there is steeply positive, not zero."],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[0,4],"y":[0,14],"xstep":1,"ystep":2,"xlabel":"time / s","ylabel":"velocity / m s⁻¹","lines":[{"pts":[[0.0,0.0],[0.025,0.298125],[0.05,0.5925],[0.075,0.883125],[0.1,1.17],[0.125,1.453125],[0.15,1.7325],[0.175,2.008125],[0.2,2.28],[0.225,2.548125],[0.25,2.8125],[0.275,3.073125],[0.3,3.33],[0.325,3.583125],[0.35,3.8325],[0.375,4.078125],[0.4,4.32],[0.425,4.558125],[0.45,4.7925],[0.475,5.023125],[0.5,5.25],[0.525,5.473125],[0.55,5.6925],[0.575,5.908125],[0.6,6.12],[0.625,6.328125],[0.65,6.5325],[0.675,6.733125],[0.7,6.93],[0.725,7.123125],[0.75,7.3125],[0.775,7.498125],[0.8,7.68],[0.825,7.858125],[0.85,8.0325],[0.875,8.203125],[0.9,8.37],[0.925,8.533125],[0.95,8.6925],[0.975,8.848125],[1.0,9.0],[1.025,9.148125],[1.05,9.2925],[1.075,9.433125],[1.1,9.57],[1.125,9.703125],[1.15,9.8325],[1.175,9.958125],[1.2,10.08],[1.225,10.198125],[1.25,10.3125],[1.275,10.423125],[1.3,10.53],[1.325,10.633125],[1.35,10.7325],[1.375,10.828125],[1.4,10.92],[1.425,11.008125],[1.45,11.0925],[1.475,11.173125],[1.5,11.25],[1.525,11.323125],[1.55,11.3925],[1.575,11.458125],[1.6,11.52],[1.625,11.578125],[1.65,11.6325],[1.675,11.683125],[1.7,11.73],[1.725,11.773125],[1.75,11.8125],[1.775,11.848125],[1.8,11.88],[1.825,11.908125],[1.85,11.9325],[1.875,11.953125],[1.