{"id":"ma-fig-029","s":"maths","t":"p1-14","lv":2,"q":"The graph shows $y=a^x$ for a constant $a>0$. Use the coordinates of the marked point P to find $a$.","o":["$2$","$\\frac{1}{2}$","$\\frac{1}{4}$","$4$"],"a":1,"x":"P is at $x=-2$, $y=4$, so $a^{-2}=4$. Then $a^2=\\frac14$ and $a=\\frac12$. The curve falls as $x$ increases, which agrees with $0<a<1$.","w":["Treated $a^{-2}=4$ as $a^2=4$, ignoring the negative index, so the curve would rise.","","Wrote $a=4^{-1}$ instead of $4^{-1/2}$, forgetting that the index is $-2$ rather than $-1$.","Took the $y$-value of P as $a$. The $y$-value is $a^{-2}$, not $a$."],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[-3,3],"y":[0,8],"xstep":1,"ystep":1,"xlabel":"x","ylabel":"y","lines":[{"pts":[[-3.0,8.0],[-2.9625,7.794735],[-2.925,7.594737],[-2.8875,7.39987],[-2.85,7.210004],[-2.8125,7.025009],[-2.775,6.84476],[-2.7375,6.669137],[-2.7,6.498019],[-2.6625,6.331292],[-2.625,6.168843],[-2.5875,6.010562],[-2.55,5.856343],[-2.5125,5.70608],[-2.475,5.559673],[-2.4375,5.417022],[-2.4,5.278032],[-2.3625,5.142607],[-2.325,5.010658],[-2.2875,4.882094],[-2.25,4.756828],[-2.2125,4.634777],[-2.175,4.515858],[-2.1375,4.399989],[-2.1,4.287094],[-2.0625,4.177095],[-2.025,4.069919],[-1.9875,3.965492],[-1.95,3.863745],[-1.9125,3.764609],[-1.875,3.668016],[-1.8375,3.573902],[-1.8,3.482202],[-1.7625,3.392856],[-1.725,3.305801],[-1.6875,3.220981],[-1.65,3.138336],[-1.6125,3.057813],[-1.575,2.979355],[-1.5375,2.90291],[-1.5,2.828427],[-1.4625,2.755855],[-1.425,2.685145],[-1.3875,2.616249],[-1.35,2.549121],[-1.3125,2.483716],[-1.275,2.419988],[-1.2375,2.357896],[-1.2,2.297397],[-1.1625,2.23845],[-1.125,2.181015],[-1.0875,2.125055],[-1.05,2.07053],[-1.0125,2.017404],[-0.975,1.965641],[-0.9375,1.915207],[-0.9,1.866066],[-0.8625,1.818186],[-0.825,1.771535],[-0.7875,1.726081],[-0.75,1.681793],[-0.7125,1.638641],[-0.675,1.596597],[-0.6375,1.555631],[-0.6,1.515717],[-0.5625,1.476826],[-0.525,1.438934],[-0.4875,1.402013],[-0.45,1.36604],[-0.4125,1.33099],[-0.375,1.29684],[-0.