{"id":"ma-fig-069","s":"maths","t":"p1-09","lv":2,"q":"The line $y=k$ meets the curve $y=\\sin x$ (x in degrees) at P and Q. Use the graph to find $k$, then give the $x$-coordinates of P and Q.","o":["$30^\\circ$ and $330^\\circ$","$60^\\circ$ and $120^\\circ$","$30^\\circ$ and $150^\\circ$","$30^\\circ$ and $210^\\circ$"],"a":2,"x":"The line crosses the vertical axis at $0.5$, so $k=0.5$. Then $\\sin^{-1}0.5=30^\\circ$. The curve is symmetric about $x=90^\\circ$, so the other solution is $180^\\circ-30^\\circ=150^\\circ$.","w":["Used $360^\\circ-30^\\circ$, which is the second solution for $\\cos x=0.5$, not for $\\sin x=0.5$.","Took $\\sin 60^\\circ=0.5$, mixing up the exact values of sine and cosine, then reflected about $90^\\circ$.","","Used $180^\\circ+30^\\circ$, which gives a negative sine. The line is above the axis, so both points are in the first half of the cycle."],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[0,360],"y":[-1,1],"xstep":90,"ystep":0.25,"xlabel":"x / degrees","ylabel":"y","lines":[{"pts":[[0.0,0.0],[2.25,0.03926],[4.5,0.078459],[6.75,0.117537],[9.0,0.156434],[11.25,0.19509],[13.5,0.233445],[15.75,0.27144],[18.0,0.309017],[20.25,0.346117],[22.5,0.382683],[24.75,0.41866],[27.0,0.45399],[29.25,0.488621],[31.5,0.522499],[33.75,0.55557],[36.0,0.587785],[38.25,0.619094],[40.5,0.649448],[42.75,0.678801],[45.0,0.707107],[47.25,0.734323],[49.5,0.760406],[51.75,0.785317],[54.0,0.809017],[56.25,0.83147],[58.5,0.85264],[60.75,0.872496],[63.0,0.891007],[65.25,0.908143],[67.5,0.92388],[69.75,0.938191],[72.0,0.951057],[74.25,0.962455],[76.5,0.97237],[78.75,0.980785],[81.0,0.987688],[83.25,0.993068],[85.5,0.996917],[87.75,0.999229],[90.0,1.0],[92.25,0.999229],[94.5,0.996917],[96.75,0.993068],[99.0,0.987688],[101.25,0.980785],[103.5,0.97237],[105.75,0.962455],[108.0,0.951057],[110.25,0.938191],[112.5,0.92388],[114.75,0.908143],[117.0,0.891007],[119.25,0.872496],[121.5,0.85264],[123.75,0.83147],[126.0,0.809017],[128.25,0.785317],[130.5,0.760406],[132.75,0.734323],[135.0,0.70