{"id":"ma-fig-066","s":"maths","t":"p1-03","lv":2,"q":"Curve C has equation $y=x^2-4x+3$. The graph shows C and the straight line L, which meet at P and Q. Which equation in $x$ has the $x$-coordinates of P and Q as its roots?","o":["$x^2-5x+4=0$","$x^2-4x+3=0$","$x^2-5x+2=0$","$x^2-3x+4=0$"],"a":0,"x":"L passes through $(0,-1)$ and $(1,0)$, so its gradient is 1 and its equation is $y=x-1$. Equate: $x^2-4x+3=x-1$, so $x^2-5x+4=0$, with roots 1 and 4 matching P and Q.","w":["","This sets $y=0$ and finds where C crosses the $x$-axis, ignoring line L completely.","The $y$-intercept of L was read as $+1$ instead of $-1$, giving $y=x+1$.","The gradient of L was taken as $-1$, giving $y=-x-1$, so the signs are wrong."],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[0,5],"y":[-1,8],"xstep":1,"ystep":1,"xlabel":"x","ylabel":"y","lines":[{"pts":[[0.0,3.0],[0.03125,2.875977],[0.0625,2.753906],[0.09375,2.633789],[0.125,2.515625],[0.15625,2.399414],[0.1875,2.285156],[0.21875,2.172852],[0.25,2.0625],[0.28125,1.954102],[0.3125,1.847656],[0.34375,1.743164],[0.375,1.640625],[0.40625,1.540039],[0.4375,1.441406],[0.46875,1.344727],[0.5,1.25],[0.53125,1.157227],[0.5625,1.066406],[0.59375,0.977539],[0.625,0.890625],[0.65625,0.805664],[0.6875,0.722656],[0.71875,0.641602],[0.75,0.5625],[0.78125,0.485352],[0.8125,0.410156],[0.84375,0.336914],[0.875,0.265625],[0.90625,0.196289],[0.9375,0.128906],[0.96875,0.063477],[1.0,0.0],[1.03125,-0.061523],[1.0625,-0.121094],[1.09375,-0.178711],[1.125,-0.234375],[1.15625,-0.288086],[1.1875,-0.339844],[1.21875,-0.389648],[1.25,-0.4375],[1.28125,-0.483398],[1.3125,-0.527344],[1.34375,-0.569336],[1.375,-0.609375],[1.40625,-0.647461],[1.4375,-0.683594],[1.46875,-0.717773],[1.5,-0.75],[1.53125,-0.780273],[1.5625,-0.808594],[1.59375,-0.834961],[1.625,-0.859375],[1.65625,-0.881836],[1.6875,-0.902344],[1.71875,-0.920898],[1.75,-0.9375],[1.78125,-0.952148],[1.8125,-0.964844],[1.84375,-0.975586],[1.875,-0.984375],[1.90625,-0.991211],[1.9375,-0.996094],[1.96875,-0.999023],[2.0,-1.0]