{"id":"ma-fig-067","s":"maths","t":"p1-03","lv":3,"q":"On the graph, a point satisfies the inequalities if it is on or below the solid curve and also strictly above the dashed line. Which marked point satisfies both?","o":["P","Q","R","S"],"a":2,"x":"The solid curve includes points on it; the dashed line excludes points on it. R $(0,4)$ lies on the curve and above the line, so it satisfies both. Q is on the dashed line.","w":["P $(-2,2)$ is above the solid curve, which is $y=0$ at $x=-2$, so it fails the first inequality.","Q $(2,0)$ is on the curve but also on the dashed line. A dashed boundary is not included, so Q fails.","","S $(1,-2)$ is under the curve but below the dashed line, which is at $y=-1$ when $x=1$, so it fails."],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[-3,3],"y":[-6,6],"xstep":1,"ystep":2,"xlabel":"x","ylabel":"y","lines":[{"pts":[[-3.0,-5.0],[-2.9625,-4.776406],[-2.925,-4.555625],[-2.8875,-4.337656],[-2.85,-4.1225],[-2.8125,-3.910156],[-2.775,-3.700625],[-2.7375,-3.493906],[-2.7,-3.29],[-2.6625,-3.088906],[-2.625,-2.890625],[-2.5875,-2.695156],[-2.55,-2.5025],[-2.5125,-2.312656],[-2.475,-2.125625],[-2.4375,-1.941406],[-2.4,-1.76],[-2.3625,-1.581406],[-2.325,-1.405625],[-2.2875,-1.232656],[-2.25,-1.0625],[-2.2125,-0.895156],[-2.175,-0.730625],[-2.1375,-0.568906],[-2.1,-0.41],[-2.0625,-0.253906],[-2.025,-0.100625],[-1.9875,0.049844],[-1.95,0.1975],[-1.9125,0.342344],[-1.875,0.484375],[-1.8375,0.623594],[-1.8,0.76],[-1.7625,0.893594],[-1.725,1.024375],[-1.6875,1.152344],[-1.65,1.2775],[-1.6125,1.399844],[-1.575,1.519375],[-1.5375,1.636094],[-1.5,1.75],[-1.4625,1.861094],[-1.425,1.969375],[-1.3875,2.074844],[-1.35,2.1775],[-1.3125,2.277344],[-1.275,2.374375],[-1.2375,2.468594],[-1.2,2.56],[-1.1625,2.648594],[-1.125,2.734375],[-1.0875,2.817344],[-1.05,2.8975],[-1.0125,2.974844],[-0.975,3.049375],[-0.9375,3.121094],[-0.9,3.19],[-0.8625,3.256094],[-0.825,3.319375],[-0.7875,3.379844],[-0.75,3.4375],[-0.7125,3.492344],[-0.675,3.544375],[-0.6375,3.593594],[-0.6,3.64],[-0