{"id":"ma-fig-068","s":"maths","t":"p1-04","lv":2,"q":"The graph shows $y=\\frac{1}{x}$ (curve A) and curve B, its image under a translation. The dashed lines are the asymptotes of B. Which translation maps A onto B?","o":["2 units left and 1 unit up","2 units right and 1 unit up","2 units right and 1 unit down","1 unit right and 2 units up"],"a":1,"x":"A has asymptotes $x=0$ and $y=0$. The dashed asymptotes of B are $x=2$ and $y=1$. The vertical asymptote moves from 0 to 2 (right 2) and the horizontal one from 0 to 1 (up 1). So B is $y=\\frac{1}{x-2}+1$.","w":["Treated the vertical asymptote at $x=2$ as a shift left, confusing $f(x-2)$ with $f(x+2)$.","","Read the horizontal asymptote $y=1$ as a downward shift, when it is above the $x$-axis so the shift is up.","Swapped the two shifts, using the $y$-asymptote value for the $x$-direction and vice versa."],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[-3,5],"y":[-3,5],"xstep":1,"ystep":1,"xlabel":"x","ylabel":"y","lines":[{"pts":[[-3.0,-0.333333],[-2.95,-0.338983],[-2.9,-0.344828],[-2.85,-0.350877],[-2.8,-0.357143],[-2.75,-0.363636],[-2.7,-0.37037],[-2.65,-0.377358],[-2.6,-0.384615],[-2.55,-0.392157],[-2.5,-0.4],[-2.45,-0.408163],[-2.4,-0.416667],[-2.35,-0.425532],[-2.3,-0.434783],[-2.25,-0.444444],[-2.2,-0.454545],[-2.15,-0.465116],[-2.1,-0.47619],[-2.05,-0.487805],[-2.0,-0.5],[-1.95,-0.512821],[-1.9,-0.526316],[-1.85,-0.540541],[-1.8,-0.555556],[-1.75,-0.571429],[-1.7,-0.588235],[-1.65,-0.606061],[-1.6,-0.625],[-1.55,-0.645161],[-1.5,-0.666667],[-1.45,-0.689655],[-1.4,-0.714286],[-1.35,-0.740741],[-1.3,-0.769231],[-1.25,-0.8],[-1.2,-0.833333],[-1.15,-0.869565],[-1.1,-0.909091],[-1.05,-0.952381],[-1.0,-1.0],[-0.95,-1.052632],[-0.9,-1.111111],[-0.85,-1.176471],[-0.8,-1.25],[-0.75,-1.333333],[-0.7,-1.428571],[-0.65,-1.538462],[-0.6,-1.666667],[-0.55,-1.818182],[-0.5,-2.0],[-0.45,-2.222222],[-0.4,-2.5],[-0.35,-2.857143],[-0.3,-3.333333],[-0.25,-4.0],[-0.2,-5.0],[-0.15,-6.666667],[-0.1,-10.0],[-0.05,-20.0]],"c":0},{"pts":[[0.05,20.0],[0.1