{"id":"ma-fig-074","s":"maths","t":"p2-07","lv":2,"q":"The graph shows y = 5 sin(x + 53.13°) for 0 ≤ x < 360° and the line y = 2. Which option gives the number of solutions of 5 sin(x + 53.13°) = 2 in this range, with their approximate values?","o":["Two solutions, x ≈ 23° and x ≈ 157°","Two solutions, x ≈ 77° and x ≈ 210°","Two solutions, x ≈ 103° and x ≈ 330°","Four solutions, x ≈ 23°, 103°, 157° and 330°"],"a":2,"x":"The line y = 2 meets the curve at only two points, P and Q. P lies between x = 90° and 135°, so about 103°. Q lies between 315° and 360°, so about 330°.","w":["Solving sin θ = 0.4 gives 23° and 157°, but this forgets to subtract 53.13° from each to get x. The curve is shifted left.","Adds 53.13° to the angles instead of subtracting it. This shifts the curve the wrong way; the graph shows it crosses at P and Q.","","Counts the solutions of sin θ = 0.4 and the shifted ones together. The graph crosses y = 2 only twice in one period."],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[0,360],"y":[-6,6],"xstep":45,"ystep":2,"xlabel":"x / degrees","ylabel":"y","lines":[{"pts":[[0.0,3.999999],[2.25,4.114695],[4.5,4.223046],[6.75,4.324885],[9.0,4.420056],[11.25,4.508412],[13.5,4.589815],[15.75,4.664142],[18.0,4.731277],[20.25,4.791116],[22.5,4.843568],[24.75,4.888552],[27.0,4.925997],[29.25,4.955848],[31.5,4.978056],[33.75,4.992589],[36.0,4.999424],[38.25,4.99855],[40.5,4.989968],[42.75,4.973692],[45.0,4.949748],[47.25,4.918171],[49.5,4.87901],[51.75,4.832327],[54.0,4.778192],[56.25,4.71669],[58.5,4.647915],[60.75,4.571973],[63.0,4.488982],[65.25,4.399069],[67.5,4.302373],[69.75,4.199043],[72.0,4.089238],[74.25,3.973128],[76.5,3.850892],[78.75,3.722718],[81.0,3.588804],[83.25,3.449356],[85.5,3.304589],[87.75,3.154727],[90.0,3.000001],[92.25,2.840649],[94.5,2.676917],[96.75,2.509057],[99.0,2.337328],[101.25,2.161996],[103.5,1.983329],[105.75,1.801605],[108.0,1.617103],[110.25,1.430107],[112.5,1.240906],[114.75,1.049792],[117.0,0.857059],[119.25,0.663004],[121.5,0.467927],[123.75,0.